To calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Pos-Fil-Fly Ring, we can use the given concentration and the following steps:

1. **Convert the concentration to moles/liter (moles/L):**
   \[
   \text{Conversion Factor} = \frac{0.044 \text{ g of } \text{NaF}}{100 \text{ g of solution}}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Mass of } \text{NaF} = 10 \text{ mL} \times \frac{0.044 \text{ g of } \text{NaF}}{100 \text{ mL of solution}} = 0.0044 \text{ g of } \text{NaF}
   \]

2. **Convert grams to milligrams:**
   \[
   0.0044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
   \]

Therefore, there are \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Pos-Fil-Flg Ring.
