","The speed at which electrical signals travel through nerve fibers is not constant. Two main methods of conduction are involved: serial (non-saltidal) and serial with saltillation (saltidal). The difference is significant in speed and the type of nerve fiber it occurs in.  

1. **Non-Saltulated (Serial) Conduction**:  
   - In this type of conduction, the electrical current flows in a straight line along the nerve fiber, moving from one cell of the cell line to the next.  
