CaO(s) + H2O(l) → Ca(OH)2(s)

The balanced balanced chemical equation is:

CaO(s) + H2O(l) → Ca(OH)2(s)

The standard enthalpy of formation for each species is:
- H_f(CaO(s)) = -635.1 kcal/mol
- H_f(H2O(l)) = -285.8 kcal/mol
- H_f(Ca(OH)2(s)) = -986.2 kcal/mol

Now, we can calculate the standard enthalpy change for the reaction:

\[
\text{ΔH = H_f(Ca(OH)_2(s)) - [H_f(CaO(s)) + H_f(H_2O(l))]
\]

\[
\text{ΔH = -986.2 kcal/mol - [(-635.1 kcal/mol) + (-285.8 kcal/mol)]
\]

\[
\text{ΔH = -986.2 kcal/mol - (-920.9 kcal/mol)
\]

\[
\text{ΔH = -986.2 kcal/mol + 920.9 kcal/mol
\]

\[
\text{ΔH = -65.3 kcal/mol
\]

