The equilibrium constant (K<sub>eq</sub>) is given as 1.2 x 10<sup>20</sup>.

Now, let's set up a table to track the changes in concentrations:

|Reaction**: Fe(3)Cl(3) + 6KCN → Fe(3)CN(6) + 3KCl|
|:--------------------|:--------|:--------|:--------|
|Initial Concentration (mol/mol) | | | |
|Initial Fe(3)Cl(3) | 1.0 | | |
|Initial KCN | 0 | 0.25 | |
|Initial Fe(3)CN(6) | 0 | | |
|Initial KCl | | | |
|Change | | | |
|Final Concentration | | | |

