Now, let's set up a table with concentrations:

|Reaction**: Fe(3)Cl(3) + 6KCN → Fe(3)CN(6) + 3KCl|
|:--------------------|:--------|:--------|:--------|
|Initial Concentration (mol/mol) | | | |
|Initial Fe(3)Cl(3) | 1.0 | | |
|Initial KCN | 0 | 0.25 | |
|Initial Fe(3)CN(6) | 0 | | |
|Initial KCl | | | |
|Change | -x | -6x | +x | +3x |
|Final Concentration | 1.0 - x | 0.25 - 6x | x | |

The equilibrium constant (K<sub>eq</sub>) is given by:

K<sub>eq</sub> = [Fe(3)CN(6)] / [Fe(3)Cl(3)][KCN]^6

