     \]
   - Since \( C \) is closed, \( \text{sup} f \) and \( \text{inf} f \) exist for any bounded \( f \).  

2. **Show \( \mu_n' \) is a measure**:  
   - For any \( A \subset C \), \( \text{p}_n(f) = \text{ess} \sup_{x \in C} f(x) \), so \( \text{p}_n(f) \) is constant and bounded.  
