\]
Substituting the components of the curl:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V}(x, y) = \left( \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_z}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_z}{\partial x} \right) \mathbf{k} + \left( \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_x}{\partial z} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_x}{\partial y} \right) \mathbf{k} + \left( \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial z} \right) \mathbf{k}
\]
Simplifying, we get:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V}(x, y) = \left( \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_z}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_z}{\partial x} + \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_x}{\partial z} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_x}{\partial y} + \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial z} \right) \mathbf{k}
\]
For a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) that depends only on \(x\) and \((\mathbf{V}_z = 0)\), the components of the curl are:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V}(x, y) = \left( \frac{\partial 0}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial 0}{\partial x} \right) \mathbf{k} + \left( \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_x}{\partial 0} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_x}{\partial y} \right) \mathbf{k} + \left( \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_y}{\partial 0} \right) \mathbf{k}
\]
Since the \(z\)-component of \(\mathbf{V}\) is zero, the \(z\)-components in the curl vanish, and the \(z\)-component of the curl is zero. Thus, the curl is:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V}(x, y) = \left( \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_z}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_z}{\partial x} \right) \mathbf{k} = \left( 0 - 0 \right) \mathbf{k} = 0
\]
