The reaction given is:  
\[ \text{N}_2\text{O}_4 \rightleftharpoons 2\text{NO}_2. \]  
The molecular atomic weight of N₂O₄ is \( 2 \times 28 + 4 \times 16 = 112 \).  
The molecular atomic weight of NO₂ is \( 28 + 2 \times 16 = 56 \).  

The vapour density of the mixture is given as 25.67 at 100°C and 760 MM Hg. The molecular atomic weight of the mixture can be calculated using the formula:  
\[ \text{Molecular atomic weight of mixture} = \text{V.D} \times \text{Atomic atomic weight of the reactant} \]  
